2026-09-27T09:53:19.1539289Z Description:
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1540019Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1540464Z 
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1541201Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1542058Z 
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1542140Z Update Note
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1542327Z ===========
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1542598Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1542858Z 
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1542942Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1543147Z ================
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1543261Z 
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1543434Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1543783Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1543993Z 
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1544104Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1544363Z ====================================
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1544527Z 
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1544656Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1545032Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1545373Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1546020Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1546523Z 
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1546626Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1547028Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1547543Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1547813Z 
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1548268Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1548656Z 
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1548734Z Packages
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1548923Z ========
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1549024Z 
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1550922Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1553074Z 
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1553457Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1554211Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1626376Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1627620Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1628677Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1629568Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1630684Z 
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1630799Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1631054Z ==========================
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1631212Z 
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1632250Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1633395Z 
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1634029Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1634892Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T09:53:19.1635109Z 
